WEBVTT

c0001
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.320
Thank you very much Susan. Ladies, gentlemen, friends. My managers was the or one of the

c0002
00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:33.439
greatest men of his time. Usually we know my managers as a great legal mind. The only

c0003
00:00:33.439 --> 00:00:45.240
complete code of the entire rabbinic jurisprudence was written by my managers. Every code written

c0004
00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:58.119
either before or after comprises a small only a small section of rabbinic law. To give you

c0005
00:00:58.119 --> 00:01:06.000
an example of what the code of my managers represent, it's a book containing exactly

c0006
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:21.360
I counted 1,000 chapters. Each chapter has about 20 paragraphs. Every paragraph contains

c0007
00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:30.519
between three and five legal decisions. In other words, we're talking about an individual

c0008
00:01:30.519 --> 00:01:42.000
who wrote, established the law in about 100,000 cases. But that was only one of the many works

c0009
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:51.680
that he did. He's also known as a philosopher. As a matter of fact, they speak of my managers as a

c0010
00:01:51.680 --> 00:02:02.199
rationalist. And he was. He was a superb astronomer. In some of his, the chapters of

c0011
00:02:02.199 --> 00:02:13.119
the guide, my managers asked questions about the Ptolemyian astronomical system without giving an

c0012
00:02:13.119 --> 00:02:20.119
answer. Questions that he asked in disapproval. Questions that several centuries later Copernicus

c0013
00:02:20.119 --> 00:02:31.360
would ask. Copernicus asked the same questions, but Copernicus would come to the theory that the

c0014
00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:39.759
earth turns around the sun. What is important is that my managers in the history of science is the

c0015
00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:46.839
first one who point to certain discrepancies in the Ptolemyian system. He was a great physician.

c0016
00:02:46.839 --> 00:02:56.720
Today, we are coming back to the medicine of my managers. We believe in three major points about

c0017
00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:05.639
medicine. Number one, that medicine has to be basically holistic. You cannot treat a single

c0018
00:03:05.639 --> 00:03:13.320
ailment of the body without taking consideration the whole environment in which the individual

c0019
00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:24.240
lives. He goes to such an extreme as to, as a physician, to ask a patient the color of the walls

c0020
00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:36.279
of his house to recommend not only medicine, but also music. A holistic concept of medicine. Another

c0021
00:03:36.279 --> 00:03:44.919
point which is terribly important in his medicine is the task of the doctor is not to cure, but to

c0022
00:03:44.919 --> 00:03:51.880
prevent the human body of becoming sick. A sick person going to a doctor is a failure of a doctor.

c0023
00:03:51.880 --> 00:04:03.080
The doctor should not have allowed the patient to become sick. And last but not least, that when the

c0024
00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:16.119
doctor applies a particular cure, he should make sure that the cure is not worse than the sickness itself,

c0025
00:04:16.119 --> 00:04:26.519
the implications of whatever a cure a person might have. A man of great mind. What I want to explore with you

c0026
00:04:26.519 --> 00:04:36.679
is an aspect of my managers which is unknown. Those modern scholars who have examined the

c0027
00:04:36.679 --> 00:04:45.799
Moreh Nebukhim deal only with the rationalistic aspect of my managers. And indeed,

c0028
00:04:45.799 --> 00:04:54.200
he was rational. But there is something very important about my managers. Let me tell you

c0029
00:04:54.200 --> 00:05:06.279
first in a kernel, very briefly, what is my manager's theory of mysticism. And then I will try to show you how it works.

c0030
00:05:06.279 --> 00:05:16.079
The most important thing of my managers is that there are three stages in the human development

c0031
00:05:16.079 --> 00:05:31.079
as an individual, and in humanity as an anthropological groups. At an early stage, humanity, or we

c0032
00:05:31.079 --> 00:05:41.799
when we are children or immature, we live in the realm of myth. We are mythological.

c0033
00:05:41.799 --> 00:06:04.799
We are not totally aware of either time or space. Ideas pollute our mind. And those ideas prevent us from perceiving the real reality.

c0034
00:06:04.799 --> 00:06:19.799
At that stage, the world is anthropocentric. What I mean to say is, man, the individual, the person, is at the center of reality.

c0035
00:06:19.799 --> 00:06:38.799
When the primitive man, or we, in an immature stage, perceive the reality, this reality is a projection of ourselves. Even when we love or when we hate.

c0036
00:06:38.799 --> 00:06:57.799
Even when we speak of God, the God that we perceive at that early stage of development is a God fabricated by our own myth, by our own imagination.

c0037
00:06:57.799 --> 00:07:13.799
There is another stage, and this stage of reason, of rationality. There is a stage in which we discover that there is an objective reality.

c0038
00:07:13.799 --> 00:07:35.799
Something that does not depend on us. Texts, that there are laws, invariable, mathematical, mechanical, that did not and will not change.

c0039
00:07:35.799 --> 00:07:54.799
And then we try to comprehend this world. We immerse ourselves in the world of the objective. In the world of must, of necessity, cause, effect.

c0040
00:07:54.799 --> 00:08:15.799
But once that we course into the realm of the objective, we come at a boundary. And that boundary is what my mind has called the realm of the mystical.

c0041
00:08:16.799 --> 00:08:34.799
The realm of prophecy. There is a limit to rationality. Rationality is important, is a stage in human development.

c0042
00:08:34.799 --> 00:08:50.799
But there is a realm, much larger and bigger and complex than the world of rationality, that transcends it.

c0043
00:08:50.799 --> 00:09:10.799
And when you come to that border, the rules that you had while in the realm of rationality will no longer operate.

c0044
00:09:10.799 --> 00:09:37.799
It is a different kind of reality. For my mind it is, the difference between the world of the mystic, in that sense, is not the world that negates rationality, but rather than transcends rationality.

c0045
00:09:38.799 --> 00:09:44.799
For my mind it is the Sodot, that speaks constantly, the secrets of the Tora.

c0046
00:09:44.799 --> 00:10:10.799
The cosmology of the Tora, the chariot of the Tora, is not an anti-rational realm, but is the realm of the post-rational.

c0047
00:10:10.799 --> 00:10:28.799
For reasons that really are irrelevant at this point to explain, somehow the way God programmed the human race and the human individual,

c0048
00:10:28.799 --> 00:10:46.799
is to evolve as an anthropological group or as an individual, from the realm of the mythical, to the realm of the rational, to the realm of the post-rational.

c0049
00:10:46.799 --> 00:10:57.799
For my mind it is, you can never pass from the mythical to the post-rational.

c0050
00:10:58.799 --> 00:11:16.799
The only way to reach mysticism, for my mind it is, the mysticism of the Tora, the mysticism of the prophets, is to exhaust your rationality.

c0051
00:11:17.799 --> 00:11:36.799
And when you come to the very end of what your mind can achieve, only at the border, then you can discover another realm of reality.

c0052
00:11:37.799 --> 00:11:58.799
But, for those who remain in the early stage of mythical thinking, the world of mysticism that they have is a figment of their own imagination.

c0053
00:11:59.799 --> 00:12:07.799
Let me be a little bit more articulate and precise about my mindless thinking.

c0054
00:12:08.799 --> 00:12:17.799
There are some very important ideas that my mindless discusses in reference to mysticism.

c0055
00:12:18.799 --> 00:12:32.799
Mysticism, for my mindless, is the aim, not of the Jew, but of the human race.

c0056
00:12:33.799 --> 00:12:49.799
It means, in different words, that mysticism is an anthropological dimension, is something that pertains to the very essence of humankind.

c0057
00:12:50.799 --> 00:12:55.799
That is one point, terribly important.

c0058
00:12:56.799 --> 00:13:15.799
Second point, the passing from the mythical to the rational, from the rational to the mystical, for my mindless, is relative to the human capacities.

c0059
00:13:15.799 --> 00:13:37.799
Somebody with limited education, with limited intellectual capacities, for that individual, the passing from the mythical to the rational to the mystical,

c0060
00:13:37.799 --> 00:13:46.799
would be different than for Sir Isaac Newton or for Dr. Albert Einstein.

c0061
00:13:47.799 --> 00:13:58.799
But nonetheless, each individual, within his or her own capacities, could develop.

c0062
00:13:59.799 --> 00:14:03.799
That is another aspect of mysticism.

c0063
00:14:04.799 --> 00:14:10.799
Now, I want to be more and more specific.

c0064
00:14:13.799 --> 00:14:29.799
Briefly, the mystic is the individual who, in a sense, discovers who he or she is.

c0065
00:14:30.799 --> 00:14:43.799
More precise, the mystic is the one who forges him or herself.

c0066
00:14:44.799 --> 00:14:47.799
Let me explain.

c0067
00:14:48.799 --> 00:15:10.799
For the mythical mind, for the primitive, for those who do not face reality and rationality, to always think about some idyllic past.

c0068
00:15:11.799 --> 00:15:14.799
The paradise in the past.

c0069
00:15:15.799 --> 00:15:18.799
Oh, how beautiful things were when I was a child.

c0070
00:15:19.799 --> 00:15:24.799
Always a past, a past, a past.

c0071
00:15:25.799 --> 00:15:35.799
In Christian tradition, believing Jesus in cooperation in the Corpus Christi, would take us back into the time of Adam.

c0072
00:15:36.799 --> 00:15:52.799
For the Jew, the most important aspect of time is neither the past nor the future.

c0073
00:15:53.799 --> 00:15:56.799
The rabbis and my mothers emphasize,

c0074
00:16:01.799 --> 00:16:08.799
the most important moment is right now.

c0075
00:16:09.799 --> 00:16:14.799
And let me explain what does it mean there, right now.

c0076
00:16:15.799 --> 00:16:19.799
The moment of the present.

c0077
00:16:19.799 --> 00:16:32.799
If we believe that there is a God who started moving things at cosmological hour zero,

c0078
00:16:33.799 --> 00:16:55.799
therefore it means that every moment now is the combination, the concatation of infinite circumstances that focus all of them in this single moment.

c0079
00:16:56.799 --> 00:17:13.800
And right now you, as an individual, could do something that nobody else ever was able to do, and nobody again will ever be able to duplicate.

c0080
00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:24.800
And when you do that thing now, you change the course of the cosmos.

c0081
00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:32.800
And in a sense, you open new possibilities for new nows.

c0082
00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:35.800
The rabbis say,

c0083
00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:41.800
There is no man who does not have an hour.

c0084
00:17:42.800 --> 00:17:51.800
God never created a human being without giving he, she, gentile Jew, an hour.

c0085
00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:59.800
A moment in which he, she could do something because it's in the right place at the right time.

c0086
00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:05.800
And because he, she has certain experience or certain knowledge or certain thing that nobody else has.

c0087
00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:22.800
And when you grab the moment, you become something, someone that nobody else ever was like it or will be like it.

c0088
00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:29.800
You forge your individuality in that moment.

c0089
00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:33.800
The rabbis say,

c0090
00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:40.800
There is a man who buys his world in one hour.

c0091
00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:52.800
There are men, humans, and they tell a story about a gentile, about an inverted sinner Jew,

c0092
00:18:53.800 --> 00:19:01.800
and about an executioner, a pagan executioner.

c0093
00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:12.800
And these three individuals, each one in a different context, had an opportunity to do something.

c0094
00:19:13.800 --> 00:19:16.800
And they grabbed it.

c0095
00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:24.800
And they forged their own universe.

c0096
00:19:25.800 --> 00:19:31.800
So therefore, for my Marianist mysticism,

c0097
00:19:32.800 --> 00:19:36.800
we are not only studying books, of course we should read.

c0098
00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:40.800
The Jewish people, the Hebrew people.

c0099
00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:44.800
But all this reading and all this studying,

c0100
00:19:45.800 --> 00:19:53.800
they should eventually lead to a crossroad.

c0101
00:19:54.800 --> 00:20:01.800
The rabbis say something which baffles the mind.

c0102
00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:03.800
He says,

c0103
00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:09.800
How are we going to define a young sage?

c0104
00:20:10.800 --> 00:20:20.800
The young sage is somebody who is standing at a crossroad.

c0105
00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:23.800
What does it mean?

c0106
00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:31.800
Normally, we are objective.

c0107
00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:34.800
Oh yes.

c0108
00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:40.800
We follow the standard directions.

c0109
00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:45.800
We speak like everybody else.

c0110
00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:51.800
Statistics could tell more or less how we are going to behave.

c0111
00:20:52.800 --> 00:20:54.800
We are objective.

c0112
00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:57.800
They ask us a question.

c0113
00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:00.800
They know exactly what we are going to say.

c0114
00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:09.800
And therefore, in a sense, we are not we.

c0115
00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:18.800
We are the community of an intellectual movement.

c0116
00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:22.800
But we are somebody else.

c0117
00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:27.800
A young sage, a tamichacham,

c0118
00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:35.800
is somebody who reached the end of the road.

c0119
00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:40.800
And now the road bifurcates.

c0120
00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:47.800
And nobody else before him

c0121
00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:51.800
had traded this new course.

c0122
00:21:53.800 --> 00:21:57.800
And you have to make a decision

c0123
00:21:58.800 --> 00:22:01.800
which is absolutely personal.

c0124
00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:05.800
It is not objective.

c0125
00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:08.800
It is subjective.

c0126
00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:14.800
Nobody can teach you and tell you what to do.

c0127
00:22:15.800 --> 00:22:18.800
Because if somebody tells you what to do,

c0128
00:22:18.800 --> 00:22:22.800
it is not you who is doing it.

c0129
00:22:23.800 --> 00:22:27.800
At one moment in your life,

c0130
00:22:28.800 --> 00:22:32.800
you have to cut the umbilical cord.

c0131
00:22:33.800 --> 00:22:35.800
Take a chance.

c0132
00:22:36.800 --> 00:22:41.800
I may make the greatest mistake in my life,

c0133
00:22:42.800 --> 00:22:45.800
but I'm going to do it.

c0134
00:22:45.800 --> 00:22:47.800
What is going to be the result?

c0135
00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:50.800
I don't know.

c0136
00:22:53.800 --> 00:23:01.800
And you go through an uncharted road.

c0137
00:23:02.800 --> 00:23:07.800
Now, for my marriage,

c0138
00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:10.800
the mysticism of marriage is totally different

c0139
00:23:11.800 --> 00:23:13.800
than the qabbala mysticism.

c0140
00:23:13.800 --> 00:23:14.800
Why?

c0141
00:23:15.800 --> 00:23:17.800
For my marriage,

c0142
00:23:18.800 --> 00:23:20.800
if you could speak,

c0143
00:23:21.800 --> 00:23:24.800
if you could articulate

c0144
00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:27.800
your mystical experience,

c0145
00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:30.800
it is no longer mystical.

c0146
00:23:31.800 --> 00:23:33.800
If you could explain it,

c0147
00:23:34.800 --> 00:23:35.800
if you could say,

c0148
00:23:36.800 --> 00:23:38.800
why I did what I did,

c0149
00:23:39.800 --> 00:23:41.800
or didn't do what I didn't do,

c0150
00:23:41.800 --> 00:23:45.800
you are again in the world of rationality

c0151
00:23:46.800 --> 00:23:50.800
and you are afraid to cross the border.

c0152
00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:53.800
So, for my marriage,

c0153
00:23:54.800 --> 00:23:58.800
the most important aspect of mysticism

c0154
00:23:59.800 --> 00:24:01.800
is not the content,

c0155
00:24:02.800 --> 00:24:04.800
is not the vision,

c0156
00:24:05.800 --> 00:24:09.800
is the idea of being alone.

c0157
00:24:09.800 --> 00:24:11.800
My marriage has a beautiful description.

c0158
00:24:12.800 --> 00:24:16.800
You are in a dense, dark night.

c0159
00:24:17.800 --> 00:24:19.800
You look around you

c0160
00:24:20.800 --> 00:24:22.800
and there is nothing that you could see.

c0161
00:24:23.800 --> 00:24:26.800
And you take a decision

c0162
00:24:27.800 --> 00:24:30.800
and somehow there is a spark.

c0163
00:24:31.800 --> 00:24:34.800
And you see something.

c0164
00:24:35.800 --> 00:24:37.800
And you see something that is out of this world

c0165
00:24:37.800 --> 00:24:39.800
because you cannot explain it

c0166
00:24:40.800 --> 00:24:42.800
in your own words.

c0167
00:24:44.800 --> 00:24:47.800
The spark dissipates.

c0168
00:24:48.800 --> 00:24:51.800
You are again in the dark.

c0169
00:24:52.800 --> 00:24:54.800
But you remember,

c0170
00:24:55.800 --> 00:24:57.800
there was a moment of illumination.

c0171
00:24:58.800 --> 00:25:00.800
And in that moment of illumination,

c0172
00:25:01.800 --> 00:25:04.800
you became you.

c0173
00:25:05.800 --> 00:25:09.800
Let me explain it better.

c0174
00:25:10.800 --> 00:25:12.800
For me,

c0175
00:25:13.800 --> 00:25:17.800
the key to Jewish mysticism

c0176
00:25:18.800 --> 00:25:20.800
is in the scripture.

c0177
00:25:21.800 --> 00:25:23.800
In the book of Genesis,

c0178
00:25:24.800 --> 00:25:28.800
when our patriarch Jacob

c0179
00:25:29.800 --> 00:25:32.800
pleased the Holy Land

c0180
00:25:32.800 --> 00:25:39.800
going to his uncle Laban,

c0181
00:25:40.800 --> 00:25:42.800
Jewish mysticism,

c0182
00:25:43.800 --> 00:25:45.800
the vision that Jacob had.

c0183
00:25:46.800 --> 00:25:48.800
He saw a ladder

c0184
00:25:49.800 --> 00:25:51.800
going all the way up to heaven.

c0185
00:25:52.800 --> 00:25:54.800
And lo and behold,

c0186
00:25:54.800 --> 00:26:06.800
we are climbing up the ladder

c0187
00:26:07.800 --> 00:26:09.800
and descending the ladder.

c0188
00:26:10.800 --> 00:26:14.800
The problem,

c0189
00:26:15.800 --> 00:26:20.800
what kind of angels are we talking about?

c0190
00:26:20.800 --> 00:26:24.800
Angels, we imagine,

c0191
00:26:25.800 --> 00:26:29.800
they inhabit heaven.

c0192
00:26:30.800 --> 00:26:33.800
If they inhabit heaven,

c0193
00:26:34.800 --> 00:26:36.800
then angels of God

c0194
00:26:37.800 --> 00:26:39.800
are first coming down

c0195
00:26:40.800 --> 00:26:42.800
and then going up.

c0196
00:26:43.800 --> 00:26:45.800
But the scripture doesn't tell you this.

c0197
00:26:46.800 --> 00:26:48.800
It tells you the other way around.

c0198
00:26:49.800 --> 00:26:51.800
[inaudible]

c0199
00:26:52.800 --> 00:26:54.800
אוהלים, first climb up,

c0200
00:26:56.800 --> 00:26:58.800
and then come down.

c0201
00:27:01.800 --> 00:27:03.800
Even Gaviro says something about it.

c0202
00:27:06.800 --> 00:27:08.800
He said it.

c0203
00:27:09.800 --> 00:27:11.800
And Maimonides develops it.

c0204
00:27:12.800 --> 00:27:15.800
The angels of God

c0205
00:27:16.800 --> 00:27:18.800
are we.

c0206
00:27:20.800 --> 00:27:22.800
Something useful.

c0207
00:27:30.800 --> 00:27:32.800
And you benefit

c0208
00:27:33.800 --> 00:27:35.800
your people

c0209
00:27:37.800 --> 00:27:40.800
when you translate your vision

c0210
00:27:41.800 --> 00:27:43.800
into something that is useful,

c0211
00:27:44.800 --> 00:27:46.800
that is good.

c0212
00:27:47.800 --> 00:27:49.800
For Maimonides,

c0213
00:27:50.800 --> 00:27:52.800
if you read very carefully

c0214
00:27:53.800 --> 00:27:55.800
the last part of the guide,

c0215
00:27:56.800 --> 00:27:58.800
the ultimate purpose

c0216
00:27:59.800 --> 00:28:01.800
of mystical vision

c0217
00:28:02.800 --> 00:28:04.800
is hesed.

c0218
00:28:05.800 --> 00:28:07.800
To practice

c0219
00:28:07.800 --> 00:28:09.800
good deeds to people.

c0220
00:28:11.800 --> 00:28:13.800
Good deeds to people

c0221
00:28:14.800 --> 00:28:16.800
is the chariot.

c0222
00:28:17.800 --> 00:28:20.800
Remember the chariot that Ezekiel saw

c0223
00:28:21.800 --> 00:28:25.800
as the temple was being destroyed in Jerusalem.

c0224
